SYNOPSIS:
              Here's a simple utility that allows a global search and replace
              of distribution entries within a MAXS BBS Config File.  Spurred
              on by the recent and future developments/changes in MAXS Net.  
              Translation:  This one's for you Randy ;-]


COMPATIBILITY:
              This utility was developed on a WB2.04 A3000/040, tested on
              a WB2.04 A500 and WB3.1 A1200.  It should also work fine on a
              WB1.3 machine, given someone to try...


ARGUMENTS:  
              Typing Distributor on its own will give you a simple usage 
              template and example.

              eg: Usage  Distributor FILE1 FILE2 -D/-O ENTRY1 ENTRY2

                  FILE1   = Path and filename of MAXS BBS Config file.
                  FILE2   = Path and filename of NEW MAXS BBS Config file.
                  -D/-O   = -D Search & Replace Destination Entries, -O 
                            Search & Replace Optional Entries.
                  ENTRY1  = Distribution Entry to Search for.
                  ENTRY2  = Distribution Entry to Replace with.
                  

              FILE1 is the path and filename of the MAXsBBS Config File to
              use as the Search File, it can be any valid MAXsBBS Config File
              that has been previously used by MAXsBBS 1.51->1.54.

              FILE2 is the path and filename of the NEW MAXsBBS Config File
              that is generated by this utility.  Obviously this ensures 
              that if, (heaven forbid), something goes wrong, you haven't lost 
              your original Config File!

              -D/-O -D specifies that the Destination portion of the 
              Distribution is used for the Search and Replace.  -O specifies
              that the Optional portion of the Distribution is used for the
              Search and Replace.  Must be Upper Case, otherwise the usage
              template will be printed.

              ENTRY1 specifies the Distribution Entry to be used as the 
              Search Entry.  It must follow the following format...

              Zone:Net/Node.Point  eg: 3:30003/21.0

              ENTRY2 specifies the Distribution Entry to be used as the 
              Replace Entry.  It must follow the same above format.

              Proceeding from right to left, each section becomes optional
              as needed.

              eg:  3:30003/21 is valid, as is 3:30003 as is just 3

              Any section not specified is assumed zero.

              eg:  3:30003  will produce an entry of 3:30003/0.0


              Some examples follow...

              Distributor BBS:MAXsBBS.config ram:temp.config -D 3:30003/21 
              86:303/1.7

              Distributor BBS:MAXsBBS.config ram:temp.config -O 56:10001/10 
              333:12/345.999

              
              *NOTE* A message will be printed stating the actual amount of
                     Distribution Entries that have been changed, if any. 


TECHNICAL:    
              This utility was written in C, (3 hours code work, 3 hours doc
              work :-(), it allows the searching & replacing of four WORD 
              entries representing Zone:Net/Node.Point within a standard 
              MAXsBBS Config File.  Can't get much simpler than that...


